+        // maps code, read-only and read-write data separately, each wherever VirtualAlloc finds room. In a process
+        // whose address space is fragmented, a small data section can then land more than 4 GB below a large code
+        // section, and RuntimeDyld aborts: "IMAGE_REL_AMD64_ADDR32NB relocation requires an ordered section layout".
+        // ReserveAlloc maps code, read-only and read-write data in one allocation, in that order; a section the
+        // reservation underestimates still gets memory of its own, as before. The flag is captured by value because
+        // the factory runs once per object, long after this constructor has returned.
